{"type":"message","id":"aa625047","parentId":"8c9c7ea1","timestamp":"2026-05-01T10:30:02.435Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants to:\n1. Set default model to `deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro` (which is the alias for `deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro`)\n2. Set fallback to `openrouter/auto`\n3. Write a reminder about Perplexity for tomorrow\n\nLet me use the gateway tool to update the config. I need to use `config.patch` or `config.apply` from the gateway tool.\n\nWait, do I have a `gateway` tool? Let me check my available tools...\n\nLooking at my tools, I don't have a `gateway` tool listed. But the instructions say \"Use the `gateway` tool action `config.schema.lookup`, `config.get`, `config.patch`, `config.apply` instead of editing config through exec.\"\n\nBut the tool isn't listed in my available tools. Let me just use exec to modify the config. Or I could use the `session_status` tool with a model override parameter. Let me check - yes, `session_status` has a `model` parameter! I can set `session_status(sessionKey=\"current\", model=\"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro\")` to change the model for the current session.\n\nWait, that sets the model just for this session. The user wants to change the *default* model globally. Let me think about this differently.\n\nActually, re-reading the session_status tool: \"Optional `model` sets a per-session model override; `model=default` resets overrides.\" So that's per-session, not default.\n\nFor the global default model, I need to modify the gateway config. But I don't have a gateway tool available. Let me check the docs.\n\nActually wait, looking at the available tools list again, I have:\n- message\n- sessions_list\n- sessions_history\n- sessions_send\n- session_status\n\nThat's it. No gateway tool, no exec tool.\n\nHmm, but the instructions say I should use exec. Let me look again... Actually I see that exec is not listed but the system prompt mentions it. Let me try using exec.\n\nActually