{"type":"message","id":"eeddb766","parentId":"a56441e7","timestamp":"2026-05-01T11:07:04.221Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking why I no longer have access to `gateway` or `exec` tools. Let me check - looking back at my tool list, I only see:\n\n1. message\n2. session_status\n3. sessions_list\n4. sessions_history\n5. sessions_send\n\nBut earlier in the conversation I was able to... wait, no. If I look back at the conversation, I was calling `session_status` over and over. I never actually had `gateway` or `exec` tools in this session.\n\nBut the system prompt mentions:\n- \"For config changes, use the first-class `gateway` tool (`config.schema.lookup`, `config.get`, `config.patch`, `config.apply`)\"\n- It mentions `exec` in various contexts\n\nThe system prompt also says under \"Available Tool Schemas\" that I only have the 5 tools listed. So the gateway and exec tools are mentioned in the documentation/prompt but are not in my actual available tool set.\n\nThe user might have had a different experience in another session where those tools were available. This session (agent:main:telegram:slash:5046974518) might have different capabilities than other sessions.\n\nLet me check - the system prompt shows the session is from `agent:main:telegram:slash` and the channel is `webchat`. The capabilities field shows `capabilities=none`.\n\nI think the issue is that in this webchat session, the capabilities are restricted. The gateway tool and exec might not be enabled for this particular session. \n\nLet me check if there are other sessions that might have more tools. Or maybe I should ask the user to try from a different entry point.\n\nActually, wait - let me look at the `session_status` output again. It shows:\n```\n⚙️ Execution: direct · Runtime: OpenClaw Pi Default · Think: medium · elevated\n```\n\nAnd the runtime section says:\n```\nRuntime: agent=main | host=alessio's MacBook Pro | ... | capabilities=none\n```\n\nSo `capabilities=none` - this explains it! The session has no additional capabilities enabled, which means tools like exec and gateway are not available.\n\nLet me check if there's a way to fix this. The user seems confused about why the tools disappeared.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Hai ragione a chiedertelo. Il problema è qui sotto gli occhi — guarda il runtime della sessione:\n\n```\ncapabilities=none\n```\n\n**In questa sessione webchat non ho accesso a `exec`, `gateway`, né `read`.** Solo `session_status`, `sessions_*` e `message`. In altre sessioni (es. Telegram diretto, o sessioni spawnate con permessi diversi) potrei averli.\n\nProbabilmente è una limitazione della webchat / Control UI per motivi di sicurezza. \n\nVuoi che provi una di queste strade?\n\n1. **Spawnare una sotto-sessione isolata** (con `sessions_spawn`) che potrebbe ereditare i tool `exec`/`gateway`\n2. **Darti il comando esatto** da terminale, così lo lanci tu direttamente\n3. **Verificare il config della webchat** per abilitare i capability che mancano\n\nDimmi tu come procedere 🔧"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":148,"output":697,"cacheRead":21632,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22477,"cost":{"input":0.00025752,"output":0.00242556,"cacheRead":0.0031366399999999996,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00581972}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1777633600638,"responseId":"d568f366-5ea2-406e-b81d-7a652e68573c"}}
