{"type":"message","id":"ca54da4d","parentId":"5ec035a3","timestamp":"2026-05-01T12:00:21.741Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user ran `openclaw gateway config get` and got an error. Let me check the correct CLI syntax. Looking at the docs, the gateway command might have different subcommands. Let me check.\n\nActually, looking at the OpenClaw CLI quick reference:\n```\nopenclaw gateway status\nopenclaw gateway restart\nopenclaw gateway start\nopenclaw gateway stop\n```\n\nThose are the only documented gateway CLI commands. The \"gateway tool\" that the system prompt mentions (with `config.schema.lookup`, `config.get`, `config.patch`, `config.apply`) is a first-class tool I can call, not a CLI command.\n\nSo the user can't use `openclaw gateway config get` as a CLI command. They need to either:\n1. Read the config file directly \n2. Or I need to get access to the gateway tool in my session\n\nLet me help them find the config file. The config is probably in the OpenClaw data directory. Let me suggest they look at the config file directly.\n\nCommon locations:\n- `~/.openclaw/config.yaml` \n- `~/.openclaw/gateway.yaml`\n- Or wherever OpenClaw stores its config\n\nI should tell them to find the config file and check the webchat capabilities section.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Niente, quello è un comando interno (tool first-class per me, non una CLI). Per vedere il config, devi leggere direttamente il file.\n\nProva così per trovarlo:\n\n```bash\n# Dove sta il config di OpenClaw\nls ~/.openclaw/*.yaml ~/.openclaw/*.yml 2>/dev/null\n```\n\nOppure cerca in tutta la home:\n\n```bash\nfind ~/.openclaw -name \"*.yaml\" -o -name \"*.yml\" | head -20\n```\n\nCosì becchiamo il file giusto e ci lavoriamo 🔍"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":173,"output":402,"cacheRead":23424,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23999,"cost":{"input":0.00030102,"o