{"type":"message","id":"c082cfdb","parentId":"19c322b1","timestamp":"2026-05-01T12:02:45.868Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the full config. Let me analyze what needs to change:\n\n**Current config (relevant parts):**\n\n1. **`agents.defaults.model`** — the global default:\n   - `primary: deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash`\n   - `fallbacks: [openrouter/auto, perplexity/sonar-pro, deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro, deepseek/deepseek-v4-code]`\n\n2. **`agents.list[0]` (the \"main\" agent)**:\n   - `model.primary: deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash`\n   - `model.fallbacks: [openrouter, perplexity/sonar-pro]`\n\n3. **`channels.webchat.capabilities`**:\n   - Already has `exec` and `gateway`! So the webchat capabilities ARE enabled for exec and gateway.\n\nWait, the webchat capabilities list shows `[exec, gateway]`. So these capabilities are already enabled. But my session still shows `capabilities=none`. \n\nLooking more carefully at the config structure - the webchat capabilities seem to be defined under `channels.webchat.capabilities`. But maybe the format isn't quite right. Let me look at the OpenClaw docs for the correct format.\n\nActually, looking at the system context again:\n- \"Inline buttons not enabled for webchat. If you need them, ask to set webchat.capabilities.inlineButtons (\"dm\"|\"group\"|\"all\"|\"allowlist\").\"\n\nThis suggests the format is `webchat.capabilities.<capabilityName>: \"value\"`, not `webchat.capabilities: [list]`. So the config might be wrong.\n\nNow for the model changes the user wants:\n\n1. **Global default model**: Change from `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash` to `deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro`\n2. **Fallback**: Change to `openrouter/auto` (which is already first in the defaults fallback list)\n3. **Also update the main agent's model** to match\n\nLet me propose what needs to change:\n\n**`agents.defaults.model`:**\n```yaml\nmodel:\n  primary: deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro  # was deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash\n  fallbacks:\n    - openrouter/auto\n    - perplexity/sonar-pro\n    - deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash     # move flash to fallback\n    - deepseek/deepseek-v4-code\n```\n\n**`agents.list[0]` (main agent):**\n```yaml\nmodel:\n  primary: deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro  # was deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash\n  fallbacks:\n    - openrouter/auto                # was openrouter (bare)\n    - perplexity/sonar-pro\n```\n\n**Webchat capabilities:** - The config shows `[exec, gateway]` but I'm still `capabilities=none`. This might be a format issue. Let me check the docs.\n\nNow, I can't edit the file directly. But the user can. Let me give them the exact changes to make. \n\nActually wait, the capabilities ARE listed as `[exec, gateway]` in the config. Maybe the format should be different. Let me check the OpenClaw docs to see the correct webchat capabilities format.\n\nLet me look at the git repo or docs for webchat capability configuration.\n\nActually, let me just focus on the model change first and suggest the config changes. For webchat capabilities, I'll check the docs.\n\nLet me read the configuration docs from the OpenClaw docs directory.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Perfetto, ora vedo tutto. Config analizzato:\n\n## Situazione attuale\n\n**Webchat capabilities:** `channels.webchat.capabilities: [exec, gateway]` — già presenti! Eppure la sessione riporta `capabilities=none`. Probabile formato errato (la doc suggerisce `webchat.capabilities.<nome>: \"dm|group|all|allowlist\"`, non un array).\n\n**Modello:** confermo che default e agent main puntano entrambi a `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash`.\n\n## Cosa dobbiamo cambiare\n\nTre modifiche nel file `/Users/alessio/.openclaw/openclaw.yaml`:\n\n### 1. `agents.defaults.model` — cambio modello globale\n```yaml\n# DA:\n  primary: deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash\n# A:\n  primary: deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro\n```\n\n### 2. `agents.list[0]` (main) — fallback corretto\n```yaml\n# DA:\n  model:\n    primary: deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash\n    fallbacks:\n      - openrouter\n      - perplexity/sonar-pro\n# A:\n  model:\n    primary: deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro\n    fallbacks:\n      - openrouter/auto\n      - perplexity/sonar-pro\n```\n\n### 3. Webchat capabilities — formato corretto\n```yaml\n# DA:\n  capabilities:\n    - exec\n    - gateway\n# A:\n  capabilities:\n    exec: all\n    gateway: all\n```\n\n**Vuoi che ti prepari il comando `sed` per applicare tutto in un colpo?** Così copi, incolli, e fai `openclaw gateway restart` 🚀"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":1997,"output":1166,"cacheRead":24704,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":27867,"cost":{"input":0.0034747800000000002,"output":0.00405768,"cacheRead":0.0035820799999999996,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01111454}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1777636929002,"responseId":"cc6fb24a-5cd8-46a0-9576-c783724e3290"}}
