ight be slightly different. Let me just use a more flexible approach.\n\nOK I'm overthinking this. Let me give the user a Python script that's clean, readable, and handles all three changes:\n\n```python\npython3 << 'EOF'\npath = '/Users/alessio/.openclaw/openclaw.yaml'\nwith open(path) as f:\n    lines = f.readlines()\n\n# Phase 1: Change primary model (only lines with \"primary: deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash\")\nfor i, line in enumerate(lines):\n    if 'primary: deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash' in line:\n        lines[i] = line.replace('deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash', 'deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro')\n\n# Phase 2: Change - openrouter in agent list fallbacks to - openrouter/auto\n# Look for the specific pattern: line is \"- openrouter\" AND the next non-empty line contains \"- perplexity/sonar-pro\"\nfor i, line in enumerate(lines):\n    stripped = line.rstrip()\n    if stripped.endswith('- openrouter') and not stripped.endswith('/auto'):\n        # Check next lines for - perplexity/sonar-pro\n        for j in range(i+1, min(i+5, len(lines))):\n            if '- perplexity/sonar-pro' in lines[j]:\n                lines[i] = line.replace('- openrouter', '- openrouter/auto')\n                break\n\n# Phase 3: Replace webchat capabilities list format\n# Find the webchat capabilities section\nnew_lines = []\nskip_until = -1\nfor i, line in enumerate(lines):\n    if i < skip_until:\n        continue\n    if '  webchat:' in line or 'webchat:' in line:\n        # Check if next lines are capabilities with list format\n        if i+3 < len(lines):\n            next_lines = [lines[i+1].rstrip(), lines[i+2].rstrip(), lines[i+3].rstrip()]\n            cap_stripped = lines[i+1].strip() if i+1 < len(lines) else ''\n            if cap_stripped == 'capabilities:':\n                # Check if format is list (starts with -)\n                l2 = lines[i+2].strip() if i+2 < len(lines) else ''\n                if l2.startswith('- exec') or l2.startswith('- gateway'):\n                    # Replace the capabilities section\n                    indent = ' ' * (len(lines[i+1]) - len(lines[i+1].lstrip()))\n                    lines[i+1] = f'{indent}capabilities:\\n'\n                    indent2 = ' ' * (len(lines[i+2]) - len(lines[i+2].lstrip()))\n                    lines[i+2] = f'{indent2}exec: all\\n'\n                    lines[i+3] = f'{indent2}gateway: all\\n'\n    new_lines.append(line)\n\nwith open(path, 'w') as f:\n    f.writelines(lines)\n\nprint('✅ Config updated')\nEOF\n```\n\nThis is getting too complex and fragile. Let me use a simpler approach - just use sed for the easy changes and perl for the multi-line one:\n\n```bash\n# Backup\ncp ~/.openclaw/openclaw.yaml ~/.openclaw/openclaw.yaml.bak-$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M)\n\n# 1. Model primario (solo le righe con \"primary:\")\nsed -i '' 's/primary: deepseek\\/deepseek-v4-flash/primary: deepseek\\/deepseek-v4-pro/g' ~/.openclaw/openclaw.yaml\n\n# 2. Fallback main agent\nsed -i '' 's/          - openrouter$/          - openrouter\\/auto/' ~/.openclaw/openclaw.yaml\n\n# 3. Webchat capabilities (multi-line)\nperl -i -0pe 's/    capabilities:\\n      - exec\\n      - gateway/    capabilities:\\n      exec: all\\n      gateway: all/' ~/.openclaw/openclaw.yaml\n\necho \"✅ Fatto. Riavvia con: openclaw gateway restart\"\n```\n\nWait, for #2 I'm not 100% sure about the exact indentation. And for #3, the perl regex might not match exactly.\n\nLet me go even simpler. Use Python for ALL changes in a clean, readable way:\n\n```python\npython3 << 'EOF'\npath = '/Users/alessio/.openclaw/openclaw.yaml'\nwith open(path) as f:\n    content = f.read()\n\n# 1. Cambia modello primario (solo le righe \"primary: deepseek/...\")\nimport re\ncontent = re.sub(r'^(\\s*primary:\\s*)deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash', r'\\1deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro', content, flags=re.MULTILINE)\n\n# 2. Cambia - openrouter -> - openrouter/auto nel fallback dell'agente main\n# (quello con indentazione maggiore, prima di - perplexity/sonar-pro)\ncontent = content.r