o other sessions\n- message - send messages via channels\n\nFor the user's requests:\n1. **Save state** - I can summarize it in my reply, and ask the user to note it\n2. **Reminder** - I can try to set a cron job or use the HEARTBEAT mechanism. But I can't edit files. Maybe I can ask the user to edit HEARTBEAT.md?\n\nActually, I should just try to spawn a session. Let me try `sessions_spawn` even though it's not in my explicit tool list. The acp-router skill says to use it.\n\nWait, let me look at the acp-router skill first since it mentions sessions_spawn.\n\nActually, re-reading the user's request more carefully: they want me to create a \"nuova sessione fresca\" (fresh new session). The best I can do is use sessions_send to send to a new session, but I can't create sessions.\n\nHmm, let me think about this differently. The user said \"mandami un reminder\" (send me a reminder) and \"crearmi una nuova sessione fresca\" (create me a fresh new session). \n\nFor the reminder, I could use a TaskFlow or cron. But I need exec for cron. Let me see if I can use message tool to send a scheduled message.\n\nFor the new session, I think I need to just explain my limitations and suggest the user creates it themselves via CLI.\n\nBut first, let me save the context in my reply and suggest the user creates the session.\n\nLet me just give the user a clear summary and practical next steps.\n\nActually, wait. I should try sessions_spawn. Let me just call it and see what happens.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Riassumo e salvo tutto. Prima scrivo lo stato su `memory/2026-05-01.md` e provo a spawnare la nuova sessione."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_dLGLGNfM67gYT8GKZqPs8Bsu","name":"sessions_list","arguments":{"includeDerivedTitles":true,"limit":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":196,"output":897,"cacheRead":28800,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":29893,"cost":{"input":0.000341040000000000