{"type":"message","id":"084ee2a4","parentId":"f295e52d","timestamp":"2026-05-01T21:17:35.013Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still no exec or gateway tools listed. Same session. Let me be direct: I can't run the command. But I can help them craft it.\n\nThe user wants:\n```bash\nopenclaw logs --follow --json | jq '{time, level, subsystem, message, provider, model} | del(..|select(. == null))'\n```\n\nBut with YAML output and the message field expanded (un-escaped). \n\nActually, I don't think `openclaw logs` has a `--follow` flag. Let me check. Also, the `message` field in OpenClaw logs is often a JSON string that needs to be parsed.\n\nLet me suggest a better command that handles the message expansion:\n```bash\nopenclaw logs --json | jq '{time, level, subsystem, message: (.message | fromjson?), provider, model} | del(..|select(. == null))' | yq -P\n```\n\nBut I don't know if `yq` is installed. \n\nLet me just tell the user I don't have exec and give them the command to run themselves.\n\nActually, the warning they showed is about event loop delay - OpenClaw's main process is having performance issues. 76% CPU utilization, 7.3s max delay. This could be related to the model provider struggling or some internal processing bottleneck.\n\nLet me address both: the logging request and the diagnostic issue.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Ancora senza `exec` qui. Ma il comando te lo preparo io:\n\n```bash\nopenclaw logs --json | jq '{time, level, subsystem, message: (.message | fromjson? // .message), provider, model} | del(..|select(. == null))' | yq -P\n```\n\nSe `yq` non è installato, installalo con `brew install yq` oppure usa Python:\n\n```bash\nopenclaw logs --json | python3 -c '\nimport sys, json\nfor line in sys.stdin:\n    d = json.loads(line)\n    msg = d.get(\"message\",\"\")\n    try: d[\"message\"] = json.loads(msg)\n    except: pass\n    out = {k:d[k] for k in [\"time\",\"level\",\"subsystem\",\"message\",\"provider\",\"model\"] if k in d}\n    print(json.dumps(out))\n' | yq -P\n```\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ Sul liveness warning\n\n```\neventLoopDelayP99Ms = 660ms\neventLoopDelayMaxMs = 7.3s  ← alto\neventLoopUtilization = 76%\ncpuCoreRatio = 0.79\n```\n\nIl gateway è sotto carico: l'event loop è saturo al 76% con picchi fino a 7 secondi di ritardo. Se noti lentezza nelle risposte, la causa è questa. Possibili fix:\n\n- Ridurre i provider/model in parallelo\n- Controllare se c'è un job pesante in esecuzione\n- Aumentare le risorse se il MacBook è carico\n\nVuoi che indaghiamo il carico appena avrò `exec`?"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":289,"output":668,"cacheRead":36992,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":37949,"cost":{"input":0.00050286,"output":0.00232464,"cacheRead":0.00536384,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00819134}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1777670236437,"responseId":"313b9031-7d66-439b-9e4d-461be2bb85ba"}}
