{"type":"message","id":"d70f6363","parentId":"223b9920","timestamp":"2026-05-01T21:23:33.850Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The log file is not JSON - it's plain text format: `2026-04-27T22:15:06.478+02:00 [gateway] loading configuration…`\n\nThe user wanted to filter and format the logs. The format seems to be:\n`TIMESTAMP [SUBSYSTEM] MESSAGE`\n\nLet me think about how to parse this. The user originally wanted:\n```\nopenclaw logs --follow --json | jq '{time, level, subsystem, message, provider, model} | del(..|select(. == null))'\n```\n\nBut since the logs are plain text, we need a different approach. The format appears to be:\n- `2026-04-27T22:15:06.478+02:00` → timestamp\n- `[gateway]` → subsystem\n- `loading configuration…` → message\n\nBut there's no `level`, `provider`, or `model` in this format. The original log entry the user showed was JSON format with those fields, which might be from a different log source or the JSON is embedded within the message string.\n\nWait, looking at the user's original log entry again:\n```\n{\n \"time\": \"2026-05-01T23:13:52.745+02:00\",\n \"level\": \"warn\",\n \"subsystem\": \"diagnostic\",\n \"message\": \"{\\\"subsystem\\\":\\\"diagnostic\\\"} liveness warning: reasons=event_loop_delay...\"\n}\n```\n\nThis is already in JSON format. But the gateway.log file is plain text. Maybe the JSON logs are somewhere else, or the gateway.log has a different format.\n\nActually, the user might be seeing these JSON warnings from stderr or a different output. The `gateway.err.log` file might have the JSON format.\n\nLet me suggest checking that file too, and give a parsing solution for the plain text format.\n\nFor the plain text format, I could use:\n```bash\ncat ~/.openclaw/logs/gateway.log | perl -ne 'print if /warn|error|ERR/i' | head -20\n```\n\nOr for the error log:\n```bash\nhead -3 ~/.openclaw/logs/gateway.err.log\n```\n\nLet me also think about the diagnostic warning the user got. That specific log entry with JSON message was a liveness warning. It might have come from stderr or the error log.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Il file è plain text, non JSON:\n\n```\nTIMESTAMP [SUBSYSTEM] MESSAGE...\n```\n\nIl messaggio di warning JSON che hai visto prima probabilmente è su **stderr**. Controlliamo quello:\n\n```bash\nhead -3 ~/.openclaw/logs/gateway.err.log\n```\n\nSe lì è JSON, adattiamo il parsing. Altrimenti per il formato plain text possiamo comunque estrarre e formattare con `perl`/`awk`."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":319,"output":612,"cacheRead":39424,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":40355,"cost":{"input":0.00055506,"output":0.00212976,"cacheRead":0.0057164799999999995,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0084013}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1777670592449,"responseId":"d1f8979f-ef3b-4735-9eab-767093b65b25"}}
