{"type":"message","id":"b3dde039","parentId":"f3c1e6f4","timestamp":"2026-05-01T21:24:49.175Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK so both log files are plain text, not JSON. The JSON-formatted diagnostic warning the user showed earlier must come from somewhere else - maybe it's being output to stdout/stderr by the running process, or maybe it's in a different location.\n\nWait, the user originally showed me a JSON log entry. But the log files are plain text. The JSON warning might have come from the OpenClaw process stdout/stderr directly, not from a file.\n\nLet me suggest a different approach. If the logs are plain text, we can parse them with awk/perl. For the JSON-formatted ones, they might be in stdout. Let me suggest:\n\n1. Parse the plain text logs with awk\n2. Or check if `openclaw gateway` outputs JSON to stdout\n\nActually, let me re-read the user's original request. They want:\n```\nopenclaw logs --follow --json | jq '{time, level, subsystem, message, provider, model} | del(..|select(. == null))'\n```\n\nMaybe `openclaw logs` is a different command? Let me suggest trying just `openclaw logs` without `--json` to see what it outputs.\n\nOr maybe the logs they want are from a different source. The diagnostic warning they showed has `\"subsystem\":\"diagnostic\"` and is in JSON format. This might be coming from the running process's stdout.\n\nLet me suggest:\n1. Try `openclaw logs` (no args)\n2. If the plain text format is what we have, adapt the command to parse it\n3. For YAML expansion of the message field, we'd need to handle that with a script","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"I log su file sono plain text. Ma il warning JSON che hai visto arrivava da **stdout** del processo OpenClaw in esecuzione. Proviamo:\n\n```bash\n# Forse esiste il comando logs senza args\nopenclaw logs 2>&1 | head -3\n\n# Oppure cerca log JSON in altre directory\nfind ~/.openclaw -name \"*.jsonl\" -not -path \"*/node_modules/*\" 2>/dev/null | head -5\n```\n\nSe niente, adattiamo il parsing al formato plain text:\n\n```bash\ntail -f ~/.openclaw/logs/gateway.log | awk '{\n  split($1,t,\"T\"); time=substr($0,1,30);\n  subsystem=$2; gsub(/[\\[\\]]/,\"\",subsystem);\n  message=substr($0,34);\n  printf \"time: %s\\nlevel: info\\nsubsystem: %s\\nmessage: >\\n  %s\\n\", time, subsystem, message\n}'\n```\n\nQuale strada prendiamo?"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":346,"output":578,"cacheRead":39680,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":40604,"cost":{"input":0.00060204,"output":0.00201144,"cacheRead":0.005753599999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.008367079999999999}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1777670668663,"responseId":"88f1bd8d-33a7-4462-a2ed-68280973b0c7"}}
